# working docs (local only, not shipped)
CLEANUP_PLAN.md
HANDOFF.md
MISSING_FILES.md
AEF_COVERAGE_TODO.md
MAP_FIGURE_TODO.md

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# large model artifacts. Weights and cached predictions ARE tracked, up to GitHub's
# 100 MB per-file limit; anything above that goes to Zenodo. The only current case is
# the 461 MB full-AGBD PANGAEA checkpoint — its run config is tracked instead.
*.pth
benchmark_pangaea/full/runs/**/*.log-*

# session generator/sweep tooling (not shipped)
_launcher_tooling/

# release-assembly working doc (not shipped)
DATA_MANIFEST.md

# Bulk data fetched by the download script (see DATA_MANIFEST.md).
# The small statistics/aux .pkl and .csv under data/ ARE tracked.
data/patches/**/*.h5
data/patches/*.h5
data/patches/subsampled_indices.pkl
data/AEF/
data/weights/
data/eval_plots/

# Cached raw activations for the feature-visualisation figure, written by
# model/extract_features.py. Regenerable, and a single *_feat.npy is ~105 MB (320x320x256
# float32), i.e. over GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit. Keeping them on disk is what makes
# re-zooming/re-colouring make_feature_figure.py instant instead of a ~15 min model re-run,
# so delete them only if you are willing to pay that again. The small per-crop metadata
# (*_geo.json, *_meta.json) and the s2rgb/pred GeoTIFFs next to them ARE tracked.
comparison/maps/features/*.npy
